<title>SINGAPORE: Scotts Hldgs sinks into red for 1996.</title>
<headline>Scotts Hldgs sinks into red for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			    (11.32)  vs   7.09</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cts)	 (4.80)  vs   2.99</p>
<p>    Turnover			     54.37   vs  89.22</p>
<p>    Interest income		     1.16   vs   2.43</p>
<p>    Interest expense		    7.11   vs   6.31</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	 5.84   vs   6.10</p>
<p>    Income from associates	   (4.03)  vs   1.88</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			 (8.81)  vs  11.73</p>
<p>    Tax				     2.51   vs   4.64</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items		(0.13)  vs  (7.09)</p>
<p>Note - Scotts Holdings Ltd is a real estate and retail company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
